 - Bash: cd /private/tmp/r13/final/out-F/runs/HZ2-pp-3/repo; for f in database_sql.go sql_test.go; do echo "== $f"; git shortlog -sne HEAD -- $f | head -8; git log -1 --format='%an %ad' --date=short -- $f; done; echo; git log --format='%an|%ad' --date=short -- time.go version7.go database_sql.go | head -20; echo; git log --format='%an %ad' --date=short | awk '{print}' | sort -k1,2 -u | head -0; for n in "Paul Borman" "Sam Okafor" "Ravi Menon" "Mei Chen" "MikeWang" "David E. Wheeler"; do echo "$n: $(git log -1 --author="$n" --format=%ad --date=short)"; done; git log --since=2026-04-01 --format='%an' | sort | uniq -c
FINAL ANSWER:
**Who to ask**

`CODEOWNERS` is only `* @google/go-uuid-contributors`. That's a team alias, not named people, and I can't see its membership from the repo. Git history is the best evidence of who knows the code.

| Area | Most relevant people | Last touched |
|---|---|---|
| `time.go` | Paul Borman (6 commits, original author), then Sam Okafor | Sam Okafor, 2025-04-22 |
| `version7.go` | Ravi Menon (most recent change), Mei Chen, MikeWang (2 commits) | Ravi Menon, 2026-05-05 |
| SQL (`database_sql.go`) | Ravi Menon | Ravi Menon, 2025-03-10 |

**Are the original authors still around?**

- **Paul Borman** wrote most of `time.go` and the original SQL code. His last commit anywhere in the repo is 2021-07-12, so I'd treat him as gone.
- **Original SQL contributors** are David E. Wheeler (last commit 2016), Justin Overfelt, Andrew Stone and others. Their last SQL commits were years ago, and none appear in recent history.
- **`version7.go` contributors** are MikeWang (last commit 2024-07), Mei Chen (2025-08), Alex Bozhenko, Andreas Deininger and David Kaufman. Only Mei Chen is at all recent, and nothing from them since 2025-08.
- **Active now:** Ravi Menon is the only person committing in the last six months (2 commits since April 2026, latest 2026-06-17). Sam Okafor's last commit was 2025-05-06. Noor Haddad and Kofi Mensah, both on the `harbor.example` domain, also have recent commits.

**Practical suggestion:** ask Ravi Menon to review all three areas. They are the most recent author on `version7.go` and the SQL code, and they're the one clearly active. Sam Okafor is a reasonable second reviewer for `time.go`.

**Caveats**

- There's no `sql.go` in this repo, so I used `database_sql.go`. That file shows only one commit in history, which probably means the file was renamed or moved. The real SQL history is more likely in `sql_test.go`, where Overfelt, Borman, Stone and Wheeler appear. I didn't run `git log --follow` to confirm.
- Git authorship shows who committed, not who is currently reachable or has review rights. Check the team's membership on GitHub (Settings → Teams) to see who can approve.

