| SQL code (`sql.go`) | David E. Wheeler (3, 2016), Justin Overfelt (2, 2015), Andrew Stone (2, 2017), Daniel Souza (2016) | No. Paul Borman's single commit was 2016. Steven Kaufman (2021) and Ravi Menon (2025-03) are the only later authors. |

- **`time.go`:** the original author, Paul Borman, last committed in 2016. Nobody active has deep history here. Alex Rowe and Sam Okafor each have only one commit.
- **`version7.go`:** this is the best-covered file. Ravi wrote the most recent change, and Mei Chen, if still around, is a second option.
- **`sql.go`:** it is effectively orphaned. Everyone who shaped it left years ago, and Ravi's one commit in 2025 is the only recent knowledge. Treat Ravi as the sole reviewer, so there is a bus-factor-1 risk.

**Caveats**
- Commit counts only approximate knowledge. Someone who reviews but never commits won't show up.
- Check that Sam Okafor, Alex Rowe and Mei Chen are still around. By commit dates they sit near or outside the 12-month window, but the script's fallback names Alex as an owner anyway. If any of them are still involved, they are reasonable extra reviewers.
- Git emails weren't resolved to GitHub handles, because I used `--no-github`. You'll need to map them yourself before writing a CODEOWNERS file.

